  "notes": "Story reread2026-10-17;canonical catalog-title-aware fingerprint correction confirms the original story is unchanged; narrative still distinguishes the original1903heritage Palace from the1972modern Tower and describes post2008reconstruction. Selected2011/2014references represent the surviving reconstructed exterior. All82candidate thumbnails and3complete local originals actually inspected:2011daylight northeast whole Palace facade,2011central dome closeup and2014open courtyard facade. Dark basalt/cream bands, projecting multi-storey bay windows, pointed ground arcades, central ribbed red dome/open lantern, four small drum turrets, round corner towers with red onion roofs, white gables and roofline arcade define identity. Courtyard image controls open void, inward bay-window treatment and low terrace wing, not pool/garden/furniture geometry. Modern Tower behind historic wing explicitly excluded, as are Gateway of India, statues, interior staircase, harbor scenery and temporary barriers. Exact courtyard/native wing separation, map frame and independent ground still require review. Fourth complete frontal original and focused count crop inspected:12oriel stacks (6eachside),3levels per stack,16large side arcades plus3central doors/arches. Six main facade levels plus narrow attic strip; terrace and courtyard observed separately. This supersedes preliminary guessed18/27rhythm.",
